      "content": "The slicing motion makes sense, but I feel like I'm already doing that. I've been using a very shallow angle for the slice to ensure it's cutting rather than pushing.\n\nSince you're suggesting 28 to 32 degrees, I'm wondering if there's something deeper going on with the tool's geometry itself. Besides the bevel angle, could the profile of the tip—like how much it's rounded or if it's too blunt—be influencing how the load is distributed across those latewood fibers? I'm looking for the most precise way to handle this so the structural integrity of the pins isn't compromised.",
